export anchor NightShiftClinicalStyle:
    number: 238
    screen: ProjectsDashboard
    name: Night shift clinical
    idea:
        A calm dark teal shift board made for reading at 3 in the morning,
        with large legible type, figures shown as quiet readouts down a
        station column, projects as roomy bed style cards, a soft monitor
        trace for the fortnight and handover notes for activity.
    base: dark
    palette:
        ward: #0b1a1d, the page and the style sheet
        station: #0f2226, the header, the tab bar and the station column
        card: #13292d, project cards, readouts and panels
        raised: #1a3439, bar tracks, the current tab, the search field and note times
        line: #2a4a50, borders and dividers
        ink: #dcebe9, text and figures, softened from white to cut glare
        muted: #9dbcb9, labels, meta and axis text
        teal: #6fd3c6, the primary button, bars, this week trace, the current tab edge and focus
        tealInk: #062a27, text on teal
        dimTrace: #5f8f8b, the last week trace
        notice: #262718, the gentle overdue notice background
        ok: #86d9a8, On track text and check circle
        risk: #efc98a, At risk text, triangle and the notice edge
        bad: #f2a7a0, Behind and overdue text, crossed square and clock
    type:
        One highly legible stack, Atkinson Hyperlegible, Verdana, Segoe UI,
        sans-serif, with Cascadia Mono, Consolas, ui-monospace for note times.
        Base 17px at 1.6 and nothing smaller than 15px. The greeting is 30px
        at 700, readouts 36px at 700 with tabular numbers, card titles 20px at
        700, field labels 15px at 700 in muted.
    layout:
        A station header holds a rounded teal mark, the Brightwork name, a
        wide search field, a bell, a teal New project button and Mara Okafor
        with a round initials disc. Under it a tab bar of six large tabs, each
        an icon above its word, Home current on a raised fill with a 3px teal
        top edge. The body has two columns. The 320px station column on the
        left holds the greeting Hello, Mara, the date, a gentle notice card
        with a muted amber left edge reading 4 tasks are overdue with a clock
        and a View tasks link, then the four figures as readout rows, a muted
        label at left and a 36px figure at right, divided by lines. The wide
        right column holds the six projects as two columns of roomy cards,
        each with the name, category, a status badge, a 14px rounded bar with
        the percent at its end, and two labelled fields for tasks and due
        date. Below sit the chart as a monitor style trace across all fourteen
        days on a faint grid, with the week split by a gap, last week dim and
        this week bright teal with dots and values, and the handover notes,
        each with a mono time on a raised block, the event and its project.
        Below 900px the station column moves above the cards, below 600px the
        tabs become a three by two grid and cards go to one column.
    spacing:
        An 8px unit. 24px card padding, 20px row padding in readouts, 24px
        gaps, 48px minimum targets.
    density: Low. Large type and roomy cards so nothing is misread when tired.
    corners: Gentle. 12px cards, 10px buttons and fields, round bars and badges.
    borders:
        1px line on cards and readout dividers. The notice has a 4px muted
        amber left edge and the current tab a 3px teal top edge.
    shadows: None. Glare is the enemy, so depth is a small step in teal greys.
    icons:
        Rounded line icons at 2px stroke, 20px in tabs, sized to text
        elsewhere. Status uses a check circle, a triangle with a bang and a
        crossed square, always with the word, overdue a clock.
    focus: A 3px teal outline offset 3px, thick enough to find at a glance.
    tone: Gentle and clear, such as Hello, Mara, Handover notes and 4 tasks are overdue.
